# GitHub sync

Whenever project work produces meaningful file changes (features, fixes, content, docs, or cleanup the user requested), **commit and push to `origin`** as part of finishing the task.

- Do not wait for a separate "pode fazer commit/push" message — this permission is standing.
- Follow the normal git safety protocol (no force push to main/master, no config changes, no secrets).
- Use clear commit messages focused on why.
- After push, briefly confirm with the repo URL when relevant.
- Skip only trivial or incomplete WIP if the user is mid-instruction and more steps are clearly coming in the same turn; otherwise sync when the requested work is done.
